<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_PyrelandsIgniters_Comps.xml    PYRELANDS_MECHANICS_1 · 2026-09-11
  moved into mandrake.rm.pyrelands, PYRELANDS_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 §6 · 2026-09-25
  ============================================================================
  Attaches this mod's comps to the two igniter defs, RM_FireHawk and
  RM_FurnaceBeast, which since PYRELANDS_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 live in THIS mod
  (Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RM_PyrelandsFauna.xml).

  The patch is unconditional. It used to sit inside a PatchOperationFindMod on
  "RimUtinni Patches (Jawa campaign)" from when the defs lived there; after the
  defs moved here that gate meant a standalone Pyrelands shipped a fire-hawk
  that never carries an ember and a furnace-beast with no warmth, bed ignition
  or thermal cycle (review 2026-10-15). The defs are ours, so a failed match
  here is a real error and is allowed to log one.

  Kept as a patch rather than inline <comps> only to keep the mechanism notes
  below beside the comps they describe.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- ============================================================
             THE FIRE-HAWK (§7c). One comp, and it is only a marker plus a
             cooldown clock: the behaviour is the think-tree job-giver.
             🔴 Spread-only, never ex nihilo — the hawk cannot start a fire,
             only move one. That law lives in the job-giver's first gate;
             scanRadius here is how far it may look for a fire to steal from,
             NOT a chance to light one.
        ============================================================ -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_FireHawk"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <comps>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.Pyrelands.CompProperties_FireHawkSpread">
                <scanRadius>18</scanRadius>
                <spreadDistance>6</spreadDistance>
                <startFireSize>0.1</startFireSize>
              </li>
            </comps>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- ============================================================
             THE FURNACE-BEAST (§8b, §8c). Three comps, two of them the
             thermal circuit's two honest halves:

             1. CompProperties_HeatPusher — VANILLA. This is the enclosed-space
                half and it is free: a beast that wanders into a barn, a canyon
                room or a walled waystation genuinely heats it, because the
                vanilla temperature model spends pushed heat on the containing
                room. Calibrated against Campfire (MEASURED: heatPerSecond 21,
                heatPushMaxTemperature 28) — a little under a campfire, and it
                stops pushing once the room is comfortable.

             2. CompFurnaceWarmthAura — OURS. The open-field half, where a heat
                pusher does nothing a player can feel because outdoors the
                "room" is the whole map. A local felt-temperature offset
                around the beast instead (no hediff): see
                Source/CompFurnaceWarmthAura.cs.

             3. CompFurnaceBedIgnition — OURS. The bed-down smoulder.
                🔴 NO TAMED EXEMPTION, by ruling. Do not add one.

             4. CompFurnaceThermalCharge — OURS, FURNACEBEAST_THERMAL_CYCLE_1.
                The capacitor itself: the 0-1 charge the owner's cycle runs on.
                It is also the species marker JobGiver_RUT_FurnaceThermalCycle
                gates on, so removing this node removes the fire-seeking and the
                thornvine diet along with the charge.
        ============================================================ -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_FurnaceBeast"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <comps>
              <li Class="CompProperties_HeatPusher">
                <heatPerSecond>18</heatPerSecond>
                <heatPushMaxTemperature>24</heatPushMaxTemperature>
              </li>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.Pyrelands.CompProperties_FurnaceWarmthAura" />
              <li Class="RimMandrake.Pyrelands.CompProperties_FurnaceBedIgnition" />
              <li Class="RimMandrake.Pyrelands.CompProperties_FurnaceThermalCharge" />
            </comps>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
